<title>UK: Italian fashion guru Versace to float firm-paper.</title>
<headline>Italian fashion guru Versace to float firm-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flamboyant Italian fashion designer Gianni Versace plans to float his company on the New York and Milan stock exchanges, the Financial Times reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said Versace, whose clients include pop stars Madonna, Elton John and Sting, would float his company this spring.</p>
<p>Versace confirmed he would float his company but did not give details, the paper said.</p>
<p>Versace recorded a turnover of 560.7 million pounds ($894.1 million) in 1995 and it was believed to have risen in 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717  ($ = 0.624 British Pounds) ($1=.6271 Pound)</p>
